tic peninsula on a  greenpeace ship called the arctic  sunrise scientists will be assessing the  climate crisis impacts on penguin  colonies after other groups in the area  have collapsed over the past 50 years  their arrival is in time for penguin  awareness day on thursday which aims to  raise awareness for the conservation of  the species habitat  now do stay tuned coming up here on the  daily climate show i'll be joined by  author and presenter zayatong and  lecturer in climate law at edinburgh  university navraj singh gali and we're  going to be discussing the policing bill  and its effect on the climate protest  movement and is the global political and  diplomatic system equipped to deal with  the challenge of climate change  hello and welcome back to the daily  climate show on sky news now we're  getting straight to discussing the  climate issues of the day now with  author and presenter zia tong and  lecturer in climate law at edinburgh  university navraj singh gali so very  good evening to both of you nice to see  you both  so first of all the policing bill is  being debated in the house of lords  today and it's provoked much debate and  indeed protest the government stands  accused of wanting to stifle peaceful  protests with the legislation which was  proposed in part at least in reaction to  insulate britain protesters disrupting  commuters last year so is this kind of  legislation really a threat to peaceful  protests  and how important is the role of protest  in the climate context anyway  navrati to you first of all what impact  do you think this policing bill could  have on future protests and on the  broader climate movement  thank you um so this is a pretty uh  intrusive piece of legislation that i  think has been  fairly poorly drafted and um certainly  hasn't had the opportunity for proper  scrutiny  one of the risks of it is it's  huge breadth the bill doesn't just deal  with climate or environmental protesters  deals with matters such as road t